{"title":"PostgreSQL Internals [pdf] (2023)","link":"https://edu.postgrespro.com/postgresql_internals-14_en.pdf","date":1793769763000,"content":"<a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50361765\">Comments</a><div class=\"hn-comments\"><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=SurajMishra\">SurajMishra</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50402963\">Nov 7, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">It looks good but it's from 2023 (postgres 14). Does anyone have anything from after 2025?</div><div class=\"hn-comment-children\"><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=__s\">__s</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50403275\">Nov 7, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">To your point, PG15 has a pretty meaningful change to its base backup protocol<p><a href=\"https://github.com/wal-g/wal-g/issues/1385\">https://github.com/wal-g/wal-g/issues/1385</a></p></div></div><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=potro\">potro</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50403547\">Nov 7, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">They keep publishing Russian version of this book, with the latest covering PostgreSQL 18: <a href=\"https://edu.postgrespro.ru/postgresql_internals-18.pdf\">https://edu.postgrespro.ru/postgresql_internals-18.pdf</a><p>AI should do a decent job translating it to English.</p></div><div class=\"hn-comment-children\"><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=SurajMishra\">SurajMishra</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50403941\">Nov 7, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">On an unrelated note, this reminds me of the excellent books published by Mir Publications. Russian books in general are of very high quality.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=benjiro29\">benjiro29</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50404574\">Nov 7, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">I think this is the most up to date.<p><a href=\"https://www.interdb.jp/pg/\">https://www.interdb.jp/pg/</a></p><p>Different author but also very interesting.</p></div><div class=\"hn-comment-children\"><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=swaptr\">swaptr</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50406070\">Nov 7, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">This is probably the best and most beginner-friendly resource.</div></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"hn-comment\"><p class=\"hn-comment-meta\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/user?id=Plaoo\">Plaoo</a> · <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50403806\">Nov 7, 2026</a></p><div class=\"hn-comment-body\">Awesome.</div></div></div>","author":"","comments":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50361765","siteTitle":"Hacker News","siteHash":"37bb545430005dba450c1e40307450d8e4e791b434e83f3d38915ebad510fd50","entryHash":"577daddb461f44c3e6c2277b028b0c4d596456600ee3f53192af9340a47f6c65","category":"Tech"}